vice systems": 2,
    "■ The developed product can be used as a medical air purifying respirator (PAPR) protective device at sites with high exposure to infection, such as infectious disease pandemic quarantine sites, medical staff, and related fields.■ The developed medical powered air purifying respirator (PAPR) protective equipment does not require a cleaning process for reuse and can significantly reduce the risk of infection of the user due to the antibacterially treated material.■ Lightweight-miniaturized materials and products reduce user fatigue and improve user fatigue by applying ergonomic design.■ Establishment of essential evaluation items for medical protective equipment   - Resistance to penetration of artificial blood   - Bacteriophage penetration resistance   - Resistance to penetration of wet bacteria   - Resistance to penetration of dry microorganisms■ It is possible to easily enter the international market as a global product and competitive product by localizing the core technology for air purification and respirator and strengthening the antibacterial and moisture absorption functions of the hood and filter.■ It is expected that specific measures for performance evaluation items and evaluation methods of medical protective gear materials and electric fan main body can be prepared as standardized standards through the patent of this project: Evaluation based on evaluation items of accredited performance testing and evaluation institutions It is expected that it will be possible to apply for a patent based on this and apply it to the establishment of a standard for medical power protection equipment (material, performance, design) in the future.■ Due to the prolonged global infectious disease pandemic and the occurrence of new infectious diseases, a new market is being formed as awareness and intention to purchase protective equipment are spreading around the world. Yuhan-Kimberly Co., Ltd. is expected to establish a market for this based on distribution facilities in the global market.": 1,
    "The physical distance between the patient and the endoscopist is within 1m during endoscopy. And the risk of exposure to the patient's aerosol droplets and body fluids is considerably high in upper endoscopy. The patient may be induced cough frequently due to stimulation or aspiration during passing of endoscope through the neck, and belching, nausea, and vomiting may also occur during the examination. Therefore, it is necessary to study how much the diffusion of aerosol microdroplets can be reduced by a shield-attached novel mouthpiece compared to the conventional mouthpiece during upper endoscopy.In this study, we first designed a shield to be attached to the mouthpiece, and developed a droplet generator that can implement a situation similar to that of actual clinical situation. We performed non-clinical study using this droplet generator. The droplet volume, number, and spray distance were measured by dividing into three cases: existing mouthpiece (without a shield), existing mouthpiece and tube insertion, and a shield-attached novel mouthpiece. Unlike the two cases without a shield, in the case of the shield-attached novel mouthpiece, the droplet volume and number could not be confirmed due to effective droplet blocking caused by the shield. In the two cases without a shield, the droplets scattered over 60cm, and  the droplet appeared up to a maximum of 20cm and then disappeared in the case of shield-attached mouthpiece. The clinical trial is planned for a total of 200 patients, and informed consent have been obtained from 148 patients. We are collecting patients continuously and perfoming endoscopy.": 1,
    "A germicidal lighting has been proposed for the disinfection of COVID-19. It has been generally accepted that ultraviolet-C showed germicidal activity. However, this UV-C is harmful to human and it resulted in many restrictions for application. To overcome this weakness visible light unharmful to human is now proposed. Proposed visible lights are 405nm and 450nm central peaks, each targets 'porphyrin' and 'flavin' in bacterial or virus cell to be photo-activated giving rise to Reactive Oxygen Species(ROS), which in turn would kill harmful bacteria or virus. To realize this scheme an XLED(Exchangeable light emitting diode) technology was adopted to produce 405nm and 450nm wavelength radiation selectively.This new technology not only provides lighting capability but also facilitates germicidal activity. This dual features are certainly exceed the potency of germicidal UV-C light. Four different types of lighting products, including downlight, flat-pannel lightings, and stand-type lighting have been manufactured. Among these four different types of lighting fixtures, three types were authorized in their safeties and efficacy. It has been acknowledged that the germicidal activity of 405nm is guaranteed from serial examinations for all the fixtures tested. The efficacy of the fixtures for commercialization is now proved to be 5.50mW/cm2 within 100mm distance.": 1,
    "The thermal imaging system implemented through this research project complies with the US FDA's recommendations for measuring body temperature using a thermal imaging system.“Achieving high accuracy at the level of digital thermometers” and “dissemination through price innovation” and “smart prevention solution through IoT platform technology convergence” were realized.": 1,
    "1) Bluetooth patch type wireless electrocardiograph (disposable): Additional module and Holter electrocardiograph can be mixed- Ultra-small module in the form of a patch that can be attached to the human body (weight 15g or less, diameter 5cm or less)- Bluetooth (BLE 4.x or higher) wireless communication to connect with smart devices (Android, IOS linkage)2) Bluetooth patch-type electronic thermometer (disposable): Additional modules and personal medical devices can be mixed- Ultra-small module in the form of a patch that can be attached to the human body (weight 15g or less, diameter 5cm or less)- Bluetooth (BLE 4.x or higher) wireless communication to connect with smart devices (Android, IOS linkage)3) Bluetooth communication smart device interlocking modular patient monitoring device- Provide a means for patients to measure their own bio-signals anytime, anywhere in the patient's daily life without time or space restrictions using smart healthcare- Pre-developed patient monitoring system modules are included: Non-invasive blood pressure monitor (NIBP), 4-electrode 6-lead electrocardiogram (6Ch ECG), oxygen saturation (SpO2)": 1,
    "The characteristic of pneumonia caused by COVID-19 is asymptomatic, and medical clinicans can also observe it on X-ray images, but the patient's symptoms are non-specific, making it difficult to diagnose. In particular, elderly patients who are asymptomatic may die without treatment due to delayed diagnosis.  Therefore, this researcher team aims to develop an artificial intelligence-based respiratory diagnosis integrated system that includes a function to measure body temperature and oxygen saturation in a portable chest X-ray device useful for screening for asymptomatic pneumonia patients, and commercialize it as a medical device for preventing infectious diseases through clinical trials.○ Final goal: Development and commercialization of portable smart integrated diagnostic system for respiratory diseases○ Detailed goals● Development of a portable low-dose X-ray device capable of measuring body temperature and oxygen saturation● Development of smart integrated diagnostic software for respiratory diseases● Establishment of clinical and image data related to respiratory diseases● Clinical trials and licensingData for chest X-ray learning was collected in Cheonan Hospital affiliated with Soonchunhyang University, an artificial intelligence algorithm for diagnosing respiratory diseases (pneumonia, tuberculosis, lung cancer, pneumothorax) was developed in Haewoo Technology Co., Ltd. And an low-dose portable X-ray device was developed in Autom Co., Ltd. Research achievements include 4 patent applications, 3 patent registrations, 4 integrated portable generator prototypes, 1 simple detector device, 1 integrated diagnostic software, 3 related device licenses, and 1 related SCIE-level thesis. In addition, Korea. Grade 3 medical image detection/diagnosis auxiliary software Medical device clinical trial IND was also obtained.As a medical device for screening and testing respiratory infectious diseases by utilizing research results, it is possible to establish a one-stop quarantine system for screening patients at hospital visits or suspected patients, and is a preventive device that can be used in case of outbreak of various new infectious diseases.": 1,
    "This project aimed to develop a self-heating thermometer with improved measurement accuracy and shortened measurement time through the development of an optimal infrared ear thermometer structure. Algorithm development to improve body temperature measurement accuracy, development of optimal self-heating structure IR module, improvement of measurement uncertainty (within ±0.2 ℃) and measurement time reduction (within 3 seconds), development of thermally conductive plastic, two patent applications and two research publications were derived through close cooperation between the lead and joint research institutes. In addition, preparations for commercialization such as obtaining medical device manufacturing approval and submitting an application for FDA approval are complete. It is cosidered to be a successful RnD project since it achieved the RnD goals presented in the plan.": 1,
    "Block Diagram for System ControlThe block diagram in Figure 1 was designed to implement high-resolution sensing hardware using a 4x4 pixel thermopile sensing element for implementation of a 3D thermometer. It describes the interaction between the embedding program installed in the non-face-to-face thermometer system and the high-resolution sensor and the user of the thermometer. The system is configured based on the block diagram that controls the entire system in Figure 1.○ Flow chart for accurate measurement of body temperatureIn order to accurately measure body temperature, external temperature is considered, and the core temperature is calculated by correcting the temperature of the human forehead or wrist. It describes the interaction between the embedding program mounted on a non-face-to-face thermometer system and the high-resolution sensor and the user of the thermometer○ Design of a three-dimensional non-face-to-face thermometer systemAppearance 3D rendering image in design of non-face-to-face 3D thermometer systemThe structure is designed to facilitate three-dimensional scanning, and it is gently bent so that the user can easily approach and measure body temperature. Design development of the exterior structure is carried out so that the weight and center are properly held.■ Development of automatic body temperature measurement / access control system○ Development of an access management system utilizing QR codes● If the sensor recognizes the QR code given to the person entering and exiting, the temperature is automatically measured at a certain distance from the thermometer.● It is being used as an algorithm in the following order● ID for identification is generated by S/W provided by CM Lab.● Self-identification and body temperature measurement and display on systems installed at the entrance.● Naver and Kakao QR codes can be issued and used.● QR codes that can be used by different organizations can also be issued when using them as an access management systems.● Personal information is encrypted for information protection and can only be viewed by the administrator.● The automatic access management system is also available for the KIPASS app of the Ministry of Health and Welfare (Figure 5)● To enable the use of a variety of QR codes, a camera with a thermometer can be used, and the accompanying camera on the tablet PC can also recognize the QR code (Figure 5)● Facial recognition function is also used to increase the efficiency of automatic entry and exit management and automatic body temperature measurement● The measurement mode of the non-face-to-face access control thermometer system consists of three modes to increase user convenience and efficiency (Figure 6)● At this time, it is possible to use three methods: body temperature measurement / QR code check / Body temperature measurement - QR code check (Figure 6)■ Member management program● Program for integrated management of personal information used in the access management system or employee and member information of a company or organization (Figure 7 and 8)● Time information and body temperature information are recorded when entering or going to work, and other necessary information can be entered directly.● Only authorized administrators can access the information, and for this purpose, membership management programs can be used using passwords (Figure 7)": 1
